{"author":{"id":"f21006d1826991d76b358f177209294474e8c2701fc659ff8fe8b8f40ee77f55"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1772933157,"nonce":"Ccjk2toTUiMglFmh27UVgbccWSk=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOCGKeh87wz1tu","github-url":"https://github.com/git-bug/git-bug/issues/1528","origin":"github"},"title":"feat: add --raw to version","message":"FWIW -- related, in the past I asked git-annex's Joey to provide some `--version` so it would list only the actual version without any other info, so it could be included as is in a uniform fashion among version and in 'standard' ready for comparison form (as to say if current version is greater or less than some other version), hence \n\n```shell\n❯ git-annex version --raw\n10.20251029\n```\nand for some after release point\n\n```\n❯ git-annex version --raw\n10.20260213+git57-gffa771e735-1~ndall+1\n```\nwas born! ;)  \n\n(I personally just prefer more prevalent `--version` as option to the command)\n\nAnd that is where then, to a degree, having hexsha embedded is good and bad\n- good: allows for identification and exact comparison of the `--version` output alone\n- bad: comparison might be misleading since e.g. two branches/rewrites might have the same number of commits off the tag but different hexshas\n\n_Originally posted by @yarikoptic in https://github.com/git-bug/git-bug/issues/1522#issuecomment-4017691086_","files":null}]}